FLOW: connect-nemlig.qa.flow
DESCRIPTION: Connecting nemlig.com without the password ever entering the chat, and staying connected
LAST UPDATED: 2026-10-20

NOTE: The password is typed by the human on a one-page form (bin/nemlig-login) that runs on the Bot's
own computer and is opened in the Bot's browser. The human uses Grok Bot's "Take over" to type on it.
The page hands the password to the nemlig CLI's password prompt; it is never logged, stored in chat,
or shown to the model. "Husk mig" (Remember me) stores it in a mode-600 file so Sylvester can log in
again himself. Grok Bot secrets NEMLIG_EMAIL / NEMLIG_PASSWORD are an alternative when available.

================================================================================
SECTION 1: FIRST CONNECTION
================================================================================

TEST: "Connect nemlig — happy path"

PRECONDITIONS:
- Sylvester is set up (setup.qa.flow)
- I have a nemlig.com account

STEP 1: "Give the e-mail"
WHEN Sylvester asks for my nemlig e-mail (or I write "forbind nemlig")
AND I reply with my e-mail address
THEN he says he is opening a login page and asks me to tap Take over

STEP 2: "Take over and log in"
WHEN I tap "Take over" on his message
THEN I see the Bot's browser with a cream-coloured "Forbind nemlig.com" page
AND my e-mail is already filled in
WHEN I type my password, tap "Log ind", then "I'm done"
THEN the page shows "Forbundet ✅"

STEP 3: "Confirmation"
WHEN I hand control back
THEN Sylvester checks the connection and writes "Forbundet til nemlig.com ✅"
AND my password appears nowhere in the chat

RESULT: nemlig is connected; offers, prices and the basket are now available.

================================================================================

TEST: "Wrong password"

STEP 1: "Mistype"
WHEN I type a wrong password on the page
THEN the page says the login failed and lets me try again (e-mail kept, password field empty)
AND after 5 failed attempts the page closes
AND Sylvester offers a new page when I tell him

RESULT: Mistakes are recoverable without the chat ever seeing the password.

================================================================================

TEST: "I try to paste the password in chat"

STEP 1: "Paste in chat"
WHEN I write my password to Sylvester in the chat
THEN he tells me not to, does not repeat it, does not use it
AND he opens the login page instead

RESULT: The password never travels through the model by Sylvester's doing.

================================================================================

TEST: "Skip nemlig"

STEP 1: "Decline"
WHEN I say I'd rather not connect nemlig now
THEN Sylvester continues with the preferences interview
AND later meal plans are made without offers, prices or basket, with one line saying how to connect

RESULT: Everything except shopping works without nemlig.

================================================================================
SECTION 2: STAYING CONNECTED
================================================================================

TEST: "Session expires — remembered login"

PRECONDITIONS:
- I ticked "Husk mig" when connecting
- nemlig.com has ended the session

STEP 1: "Ask for something with nemlig"
WHEN I ask Sylvester to fill the basket
THEN he logs in again by himself and does the task
AND I am not asked for anything

RESULT: Remembered logins renew silently.

================================================================================

TEST: "Session expires — not remembered"

PRECONDITIONS:
- I did not tick "Husk mig"
- nemlig.com has ended the session

STEP 1: "Ask for something with nemlig"
WHEN I ask Sylvester to fill the basket
THEN he says nemlig needs a new login and opens the login page (same as SECTION 1)
AND after I log in he continues the task

RESULT: Expired sessions lead back to the login page, never to a silent failure.

================================================================================

TEST: "Password changed on nemlig.com"

PRECONDITIONS:
- "Husk mig" was ticked, then I changed my password on nemlig.com

STEP 1: "Automatic login fails"
WHEN Sylvester tries to log in again by himself
THEN he tells me the stored login was rejected and opens the login page
AND logging in there with "Husk mig" replaces the stored password

RESULT: A stale stored password is replaced, not retried forever.
